IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`
IMPORT `coa12-logic`

-- coa12-ch7-definitions.l4: the Companies Act 2006, Part 16, Chapter 7 "Supplementary provisions": s 539 Minor definitions
-- (lines 7539-7555 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1.
--
-- BORROWED TERMS. "e-money issuer", "MiFID investment firm" and "UCITS management company" are defined by pointing at other
-- Acts, EU instruments and the FCA Handbook, which are not among the sources: the borrowed answer is an INPUT of type MAYBE
-- BOOLEAN (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE as the borrowed definition says, NOTHING where it is not known), as the keel does (fork F4).
-- Where the text says "means", the definition is closed: a case outside it is JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words).
-- "qualified" and "turnover" are worked out from facts a witness can state.

-- COVERS: s 539"e-money issuer", s 539"e-money issuer"(a), s 539"e-money issuer"(b)
-- Plain gloss: a company or person that issues electronic money: an electronic money institution, or a person with FCA permission to issue it.
-- src:7542 | “e-money issuer” means—
-- src:7543 | (a) an electronic money institution, within the meaning of the Electronic Money Regulations 2011 ( S.I. 2011/99), or
-- src:7544 | (b) a person who has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8) to carry on the activity of issuing electronic money within the meaning of article 9B of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001 (S.I. 2001/544);
@ref s 539 "e-money issuer" (src:7542-7544)
GIVEN `the person is an electronic money institution, within the meaning of the Electronic Money Regulations 2011` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on the activity of issuing electronic money within the meaning of article 9B of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 539 the person is an e-money issuer` MEANS
    `coa12 either answer holds`
        `the person is an electronic money institution, within the meaning of the Electronic Money Regulations 2011`
        `the person has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on the activity of issuing electronic money within the meaning of article 9B of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001`
    -- JUST FALSE here is -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“e-money issuer” means— (a) an electronic money institution ... or (b) a person who has permission under Part 4A ..." (each borrowed answer is the other instrument's, supplied as an input)

-- COVERS: s 539"MiFID investment firm", s 539"MiFID investment firm"(a), s 539"MiFID investment firm"(b), s 539"MiFID investment firm"(c)
-- Plain gloss: an investment firm in the EU sense, other than a company exempted by the 2001 Order, an exempt investment firm under the 2017 Regulations, or a company meeting the requirements in regulation 6(3).
-- src:7546 | “MiFID investment firm” means an investment firm within the meaning of Article 2(1A) of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 15 May 2014 on markets in financial instruments and amending Regulation (EU) No. 648/2012, other than—
-- src:7547 | (a) a company which is exempted from the definition of “investment firm” by Schedule 3 to the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001 (S.I. 2001/544), ...
-- src:7548 | (b) a company which is an exempt investment firm as defined by regulation 8 (Meaning of “exempt investment firm” in Chapter 1) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Markets in Financial Instruments) Regulations 2017 (S.I. 2017/701), and
-- src:7549 | (c) any other company which fulfils all the requirements set out in regulation 6(3) of those Regulations;
@ref s 539 "MiFID investment firm" (src:7546-7549)
GIVEN `the person is an investment firm within the meaning of Article 2(1A) of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company is exempted from the definition of "investment firm" by Schedule 3 to the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company is an exempt investment firm as defined by regulation 8 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Markets in Financial Instruments) Regulations 2017` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company fulfils all the requirements set out in regulation 6(3) of those Regulations` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 539 the person is a MiFID investment firm` MEANS
    `coa12 both answers hold`
        `the person is an investment firm within the meaning of Article 2(1A) of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014`
        (`coa12 the opposite answer`
            (`coa12 either answer holds`
                `the company is exempted from the definition of "investment firm" by Schedule 3 to the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001`
                (`coa12 either answer holds`
                    `the company is an exempt investment firm as defined by regulation 8 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Markets in Financial Instruments) Regulations 2017`
                    `the company fulfils all the requirements set out in regulation 6(3) of those Regulations`)))
    -- JUST FALSE here is -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“MiFID investment firm” means an investment firm within the meaning of Article 2(1A) ..., other than— (a) ... (b) ... and (c) ..." (a firm outside Article 2(1A), or one of the three excepted kinds)

-- COVERS: s 539"qualified"
-- Plain gloss: a report (or a statement in it) is "qualified" when it does not state the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts were properly prepared under this Act, or under the corresponding legislation for an undertaking not required to prepare accounts under this Act.
-- src:7550 | “qualified”, in relation to an auditor's report (or a statement contained in an auditor's report), means that the report or statement does not state the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared in accordance with this Act or, in the case of an undertaking not required to prepare accounts in accordance with this Act, under any corresponding legislation under which it is required to prepare accounts;
@ref s 539 "qualified" (src:7550-7550)
GIVEN `the report or statement states the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared in accordance with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking is not required to prepare accounts in accordance with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report or statement states the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared under the corresponding legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 539 the report or statement is qualified` MEANS
    IF `the undertaking is not required to prepare accounts in accordance with this Act`
    THEN IF `the report or statement states the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared under the corresponding legislation`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“qualified” ... means that the report or statement does not state the auditor's unqualified opinion ..., under any corresponding legislation under which it is required to prepare accounts" (the opinion is stated, so the report is not qualified)
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the report or statement states the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared in accordance with this Act`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“qualified” ... means that the report or statement does not state the auditor's unqualified opinion that the accounts have been properly prepared in accordance with this Act" (the opinion is stated, so the report is not qualified)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- COVERS: s 539"turnover", s 539"turnover"(a), s 539"turnover"(b), s 539"turnover"(c)
-- Plain gloss: a company's turnover is what it earned from goods and services in its ordinary activities, after taking off trade discounts, VAT and any other tax based on those amounts. Pounds sterling.
-- src:7551 | “turnover”, in relation to a company, means the amounts derived from the provision of goods and services falling within the company's ordinary activities, after deduction of—
-- src:7552 | (a) trade discounts,
-- src:7553 | (b) value added tax, and
-- src:7554 | (c) any other taxes based on the amounts so derived;
@ref s 539 "turnover" (src:7551-7554)
GIVEN `the amounts derived from the provision of goods and services falling within the company's ordinary activities` IS A NUMBER
      `trade discounts` IS A NUMBER
      `value added tax` IS A NUMBER
      `any other taxes based on the amounts so derived` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 539 the turnover of the company` MEANS
    `the amounts derived from the provision of goods and services falling within the company's ordinary activities`
        MINUS `trade discounts`
        MINUS `value added tax`
        MINUS `any other taxes based on the amounts so derived`

-- COVERS: s 539"UCITS management company"
-- Plain gloss: the meaning is whatever the FCA Handbook Glossary says; the answer is an input.
-- src:7555 | “UCITS management company” has the meaning given by the Glossary forming part of the Handbook made by the Financial Conduct Authority under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000.
@ref s 539 "UCITS management company" (src:7555-7555)
GIVEN `the person is a UCITS management company, as the Glossary forming part of the Handbook made by the Financial Conduct Authority under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 gives the meaning` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 539 the person is a UCITS management company` MEANS
    `the person is a UCITS management company, as the Glossary forming part of the Handbook made by the Financial Conduct Authority under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 gives the meaning`
    -- NOTHING here is -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "has the meaning given by the Glossary forming part of the Handbook"; JUST FALSE is the Glossary's no, supplied as an input

-- COVERS-INERT 1: s 539#L7541 | lead-in: "In this Part—"; each definition that follows is encoded
-- "In this Part—" introduces the definitions above; each is covered by its own function.
